    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with a clear objective: maximize stolen base upside against high-ERA opposition. **Corbin Carroll** (87.14) is our marquee play of the day; facing a soft Randy V\u00e1squez, he is primed for a massive ceiling game given his elite sprint speed and the projected advantage at the top of the order. Joining him in the elite tier is **Mickey Moniak** (75.75), whose massive 14% boost for park factors and platoon advantage against Freddy Peralta makes him a high-efficiency anchor for the lineup. **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.13) also remains a primary target, as the favorable matchup against Singer allows him to comfortably clear the 70-point threshold for consistent scoring.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the day was the benching of **Henry Bolte** (48.45). While his efficiency score sits just outside our primary rotation, he was hampered by a restrictive #9 lineup projection, which dragged down his potential for run production. The optimizer prioritized the balanced output of **Josh Naylor** (59.34), who, despite a mediocre park factor, projects for more reliable counting stats in the #5 spot against Troy Melton. We must remain vigilant regarding **Austin Riley** (58.16); his matchup is solid on paper, but a 44% rain risk at his venue necessitates a close watch of the weather radar before first pitch. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (52.60) and **Seiya Suzuki** (50.49) face uphill battles against tough southpaws like Luzardo and Skubal, though their raw talent mandates inclusion over deeper bench options like **Travis Bazzana** or **Zach McKinstry**, who failed to cross our 40-point viability floor.",
